From 04ce90693ab632572ab4722d7b8db16bc5e72cac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joonhoekim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 05:50:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: don't wake the device over MHI from the panic
 notifier (y705 0043)

ath12k registers a panic notifier that resets the target:
ath12k_pci_panic_handler() -> ath12k_pci_sw_reset() -> ath12k_pci_read32()
/write32(). For registers past ACCESS_ALWAYS_OFF those call the wifi7
bus_wake_up op, mhi_device_get_sync(), which sleeps until the device is in
M0. In the panic notifier the other CPUs are already stopped and IRQs are
off on the panicking CPU, so the wake may never be seen:

  SMP: stopping secondary CPUs
  Voluntary context switch within RCU read-side critical section!
  WARNING: kernel/rcu/tree_plugin.h:332 at rcu_note_context_switch
   schedule_timeout
   __mhi_device_get_sync
   ath12k_wifi7_pci_bus_wake_up
   ath12k_pci_read32
   ath12k_pci_sw_reset
   ath12k_pci_panic_handler
   atomic_notifier_call_chain
   vpanic
  (then set_task_cpu / irq_work_queue_on warnings, RPMh timeouts)

On a Lenovo TB323FU (kaanapali, WCN7860) a hung_task panic after an
s2idle resume never got past this: no "Rebooting in N seconds", no
download-mode dump, a dead tablet until a forced restart. A sysrq crash
only left it after ~50 s.

Skip the wake while a panic is in progress (the non-zero return also
skips the matching release); the reset's register accesses are
best-effort there anyway. With this the sysrq crash prints "Rebooting in
10 seconds.." right after stopping the CPUs and the board resets.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c
index 893474de4..344e15f04 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. and/or its subsidiaries.
  */
 
+#include <linux/panic.h>
 #include <linux/pci.h>
 
 #include "../pci.h"
@@ -64,6 +65,17 @@ static int ath12k_wifi7_pci_bus_wake_up(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
 	struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci = ath12k_pci_priv(ab);
 
+	/*
+	 * The panic notifier (ath12k_pci_panic_handler -> sw_reset) reads
+	 * and writes registers after the other CPUs are stopped, with IRQs
+	 * off. mhi_device_get_sync() sleeps until the device reaches M0 and
+	 * that wake may never be seen: the panic then never reaches the
+	 * reboot (or the download mode dump). Do the accesses without it.
+	 * Non-zero return also skips the matching release.
+	 */
+	if (panic_in_progress())
+		return -EBUSY;
+
 	return mhi_device_get_sync(ab_pci->mhi_ctrl->mhi_dev);
 }
 
